
::Aggregate functions::
The clause that apply the aggregate functions to get a single result record for each group, is known to be
{
    ~Distinct clause
    ~From clause
    =Select clause
    ~Where clause
}

::Aggregate functions::
Aggregate functions are functions that take a ___________ as input and return a single value.
{
    ~Single value
    =Collection of values
    ~Aggregate value
    ~Both B and C
}

::Aggregate functions::
All aggregate functions except _____ ignore null values in their input collection.
{
    =COUNT(*)
    ~AVG
    ~SUM
    ~MIN
}

